<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-CSFC ups Fiat estimate.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-CSFC ups Fiat estimate.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>CS First Boston said on Wednesday it raised its 1997 earnings-per-share estimate for Italian carmaker Fiat, to reflect the impact on capacity utilisation of government incentives to scrap old cars.</p>
<p>CSFB raised its estimate to 385 lire per share from 231 lire, but left its 1998 estimate unchanged at 375 lire on the basis that incentives would not be extended and domestic auto demand would decline.</p>
<p>The investment bank said it continued to rate the stock a &quot;hold&quot;.</p>
<p>Fiat shares were up 97 lire at 6,395 by 1331 GMT.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
